                  <provenance type="#c"><orgName role="fmo" key="org_9">Conway, Caernarvonshire.
                        Cistercian abbey of St Mary the Virgin</orgName><p>
                           
                           This manuscript was listed under Conway in MLGB2 (p. 54), but no index card
                        corresponding to the Conway provenance was found during MLGB data reconciliation
                        in 2026. Compare the <ref
                           target="https://searcharchives.bl.uk/catalog/040-002049557">British
                           Library catalogue entry</ref>: 'ff. 2–37 and ff. 38–81 were produced at
                        different times, but it is likely that the latter was intended as a
                        supplement to the first part, since the layout is identical. [...] David
                        Winchcombe, monk of Hailes, became abbot of Aberconwy in 1482: he might have
                        taken the book with him to Aberconwy, where the later section was added, or
                        the Aberconwy Chronicle could have been compiled at
                     Hailes.'</p></provenance>
                  <provenance type="MLGB3_laterOwners">Acquired by <persName>Harley</persName>, 5
                     November 1723.</provenance>
